## LiveMarkdown.Avalonia v2.4.0

v2.4.0 redesigns the document update pipeline to separate Markdown parsing from the `MarkdownRenderer` control lifecycle.

**Many thanks to @JohnCampionJr for the high-quality PRs and patient communication!**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This release contains source-breaking API changes for applications that observe rendered-state events or customize parser lifetime.  
> The primary streaming API—`MarkdownBuilder`—remains supported and is still the recommended way to render live Markdown.

## Why this changed

Previously, `MarkdownRenderer` was responsible for all of the following:

- observing `ObservableStringBuilder`;
- parsing Markdown asynchronously;
- rejecting stale parse results;
- updating the visual tree;
- coordinating that work with attachment, measurement, and layout.

Coupling parsing to the control lifecycle could cause newly realized or reattached controls—especially inside virtualized, variable-height chat views—to expose an incomplete visual tree during their first layout pass. The later size correction could then produce visible scroll jumps or disturb bottom anchoring.

v2.4.0 separates these responsibilities:

```text
ObservableStringBuilder
    → MarkdownUpdateProducer
    → MarkdownDocumentUpdate
    → MarkdownRenderer
```

Parsing can now complete independently of attachment, and a prepared document can be applied synchronously before the renderer’s first measure.

## Existing streaming usage

Most applications using `MarkdownBuilder` require no changes:

```xml
<md:MarkdownRenderer MarkdownBuilder="{Binding MarkdownBuilder}" />
```

```csharp
var builder = new ObservableStringBuilder();
renderer.MarkdownBuilder = builder;

builder.Append("Streaming **Markdown**...");
```

The built-in `MarkdownUpdateProducer` preserves the incremental change information supplied by `ObservableStringBuilder`, coalesces changes while parsing is in progress, and discards stale results when its builder or pipeline changes.

## New document update model

A renderable state is now represented by `MarkdownDocumentUpdate`, which contains:

- the parsed `MarkdownDocument`;
- its source version;
- the incremental source change, when applicable.

Two update forms are available:

- `MarkdownDocumentUpdate.Full` — a complete, independent document state;
- `MarkdownDocumentUpdate.Incremental` — a state based on one exact previous update.

If an incremental update is applied without its expected predecessor, the renderer safely treats it as a full update.

Versions only need to be ordered within a single producer. Different producers do not need globally unique or coordinated version numbers.

## Caching or pre-parsing documents

Applications may now parse and cache a document outside the renderer:

```csharp
var update = await Task.Run(() =>
{
    var document = Markdown.Parse(
        markdown,
        MarkdownUpdateProducer.DefaultPipeline);

    return new MarkdownDocumentUpdate.Full(document);
});

// Assign on the Avalonia UI thread.
renderer.DocumentUpdate = update;
```

`DocumentUpdate` is a DirectProperty and may also be stored in a view model and bound from XAML. This is particularly useful for conversation history and virtualized lists: cached render state can be applied synchronously before attachment and first measurement.

A published `MarkdownDocument` must be treated as immutable.

Avoid driving the same renderer through both `DocumentUpdate` and an active producer unless later producer updates are intentionally allowed to replace the manually assigned state.

## Custom pipelines and producers

The shared default pipeline is now owned by `MarkdownUpdateProducer`:

```csharp
MarkdownUpdateProducer.ConfigurePipeline += builder =>
{
    // Configure the shared pipeline.
};
```

`MarkdownRenderer.ConfigurePipeline` remains available as a compatibility proxy.

The default pipeline is shared and created lazily. Configuration must therefore be registered before `MarkdownUpdateProducer.DefaultPipeline` is first accessed. Unlike earlier releases, the callback is not invoked once per renderer.

For a renderer-specific pipeline, assign an application-owned producer:

```csharp
renderer.UpdateProducer = new MarkdownUpdateProducer
{
    Pipeline = customPipeline,
    MarkdownBuilder = markdownBuilder,
};
```

Advanced integrations may implement `IMarkdownUpdateProducer`. Implementations must:

- publish `MarkdownDocumentUpdate` values;
- synchronously replay the latest valid update when a subscriber attaches;
- use the Avalonia UI thread for subscriptions, properties, and notifications;
- publish a `Full` update whenever no valid incremental predecessor exists.

The renderer owns and disposes only its subscription. It does not own or dispose a custom producer.

## Breaking API changes

| Previous API | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `renderer.RenderedVersion` | `renderer.RenderedTextProjection?.SourceVersion` |
| `RenderedTextProjectionChanged` | Observe `RenderedTextProjectionProperty` |
| `TextSearchMatchesChanged` | Observe `TextSearchMatchesProperty` |

`RenderedTextProjection` and `TextSearchMatches` are now Avalonia DirectProperties and can be observed or bound normally:

```csharp
var subscription = renderer
    .GetObservable(MarkdownRenderer.RenderedTextProjectionProperty)
    .Subscribe(projection =>
    {
        // React to the authoritative rendered projection.
    });
```

Dispose the subscription with the lifetime of its consumer.

## Inline-code interaction

`MarkdownTextBlock` now exposes inline-code hit testing and geometry:

```csharp
var codeInline = block.GetCodeInlineAt(point);

if (codeInline is not null)
{
    var rects = block.GetCodeInlineRects(codeInline);
}
```

The returned rectangles match the painted chip background, include its padding, and remain separate when an inline-code chip wraps across multiple lines. `GetCodeInlineSpans()` is also available for advanced integrations.

## Upgrade checklist

- Keep using `MarkdownBuilder` for live or streaming Markdown.
- Replace the removed rendered-state events with DirectProperty observation.
- Replace `RenderedVersion` with `RenderedTextProjection?.SourceVersion`.
- Register global pipeline configuration before first default-pipeline access.
- Use an application-owned `MarkdownUpdateProducer` for per-renderer pipelines.
- Cache `MarkdownDocumentUpdate` when pre-parsed history should be immediately available.
- Treat every published `MarkdownDocument` as immutable.
